## The Sanitized Production MIB Specification (PEN: 66550)
Below is the formal, compiled ASN.1 MIB taxonomy mapping structure initialized under your officially assigned private enterprise arc. All structural elements have been sanitized of explicit vendor text, replacing them with generic, low-abstraction ownership primitives (ownerOrg), while leveraging the active registration 66550 as the concrete production example.

OWNER-ROOT-MIB DEFINITIONS ::= BEGIN

IMPORTS
    MODULE-IDENTITY, OBJECT-TYPE, Unsigned32, Integer32, Counter64, enterprises
        FROM SNMPv2-SMI
    DisplayString
        FROM SNMPv2-TC;
-- Every import above is used at least once below. Counter64 is the addition
-- for this revision (see heeEpoch) -- SNMPv2-SMI has no floating-point type;
-- Counter64 (64-bit unsigned) is the widest primitive it defines.

ownerRootMIB MODULE-IDENTITY
    LAST-UPDATED "202608212000Z" -- August 21, 2026
    ORGANIZATION "Twin Cities Open Systems - Operations LLC"
    CONTACT-INFO
        "HEE Core Architecture Registry
         Email: inspector@tcos.us
         Registry URL: https://www.iana.org/assignments/enterprise-numbers/
         SOA anchor (per identity): ~/.hee/index/_.yaml#hee-soa.v1
         Honest status: this anchor file does not yet exist for any fleet
         identity (see prompts/INIT.md) -- it is a pointer, not yet a
         hash-verified root. This MIB's ownerTemporalAnchor subtree
         (heeEpoch, below) and this CONTACT-INFO deliberately point at the
         same external anchor, so authority here is circular by design:
         neither is the root: the yaml is, once it exists."
    DESCRIPTION
        "Sanitized Core Management Information Base for the HEE architecture.
         Maps deterministic operational variables directly to the private enterprise
         registration node 66550 without vendor-specific software abstractions.

         Dogfooded example, not just an internal spec: this MIB is written to
         double as a worked reference any ORG can copy to formalize its own
         ownership taxonomy (see docs/guides/EXTERNAL_SURVEY_METHODOLOGY.md's
         ORG term, DOCUMENTATION_POLICY.md's dogfood/document/example rule).

         The load-bearing example is the hee-soa.v1 hash chain implemented in
         library/py/hee_hash/soa.py: 3 legs (leg.home_fs, leg.repo_fs,
         leg.user) hash independently, combine pairwise into 3 duoples, and
         those 3 duoples combine into 1 stool root hash -- 3 legs and a seat
         make a stool. No fleet identity has completed this chain yet
         (~/.hee/index/_.yaml is absent everywhere, confirmed in
         prompts/INIT.md); contractTable below is where that chain's live
         state should eventually surface as a queryable object, once real."
    REVISION "202608212000Z"
    DESCRIPTION
        "Widened heeEpoch and contractTimeExpires from Unsigned32 to Counter64
         (Unsigned32 seconds-since-epoch hits the Y2106 problem in ~80 years
         from this fleet's real epoch baseline of 1789640000, per
         hee-core-system-architecture-manifest-66550.md -- nowhere near a
         1000-year design horizon). Added the CONTACT-INFO SOA-anchor
         circularity and the explicit dogfooding statement above. Tightened
         contractFileName's DESCRIPTION. Per PR #245 review thread."
    REVISION "202608172200Z"
    DESCRIPTION
        "Production release substituting active registered PEN 66550 matrix."
    ::= { enterprises 66550 } -- Official IANA Private Enterprise Number Allocation

-- ============================================================================
-- Core System Taxonomy Branches
-- ============================================================================

ownerFleetOrg         OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerRootMIB 1 }
ownerHumanRightsOrg   OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerRootMIB 2 }
ownerMachineRightsOrg OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerRootMIB 3 }

-- ============================================================================
-- Machine Rights Enforcement Sub-Tree
-- ============================================================================

ownerAgentIdentities  OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerMachineRightsOrg 1 }
ownerAgentContracts   OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerMachineRightsOrg 2 }
ownerTemporalAnchor   OBJECT IDENTIFIER ::= { ownerMachineRightsOrg 3 }

heeEpoch OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Counter64
    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "The absolute 0-second universal epoch baseline marker used by the unikernel
         gate to algorithmically compute time-window expirations across the fleet.
         Counter64, not Unsigned32: this fleet's real epoch baseline is already
         1789640000 (hee-core-system-architecture-manifest-66550.md's unikernel
         boot arg) -- Unsigned32 seconds-since-epoch wraps at 2^32-1
         (~2106 AD, the general Unix Y2106 problem), roughly 80 years of
         runway from that baseline. Counter64 gives ~584 billion years,
         which comfortably clears a 1000-year design horizon.
         Deliberate deviation from strict SNMP Counter64 semantics (a
         monotonic wrapping counter, not a timestamp) -- flagged here rather
         than silently repurposed, because SNMPv2-SMI defines no other
         64-bit unsigned primitive and no floating-point type at all."
    ::= { ownerTemporalAnchor 1 }

contractTable OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      SEQUENCE OF ContractEntry
    MAX-ACCESS  not-accessible
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "Live matrix reflecting cryptographically verified cross-signing agreements."
    ::= { ownerAgentContracts 1 }

contractEntry OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      ContractEntry
    MAX-ACCESS  not-accessible
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "A singular authority validation record mapping permissions to hardware."
    INDEX       { contractIndex }
    ::= { contractTable 1 }

ContractEntry ::= SEQUENCE {
    contractIndex           Integer32,
    contractFileName        DisplayString,
    contractType            INTEGER,
    contractTimeExpires     Counter64,
    contractStatus          INTEGER
}

contractIndex OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Integer32 (1..2147483647)
    MAX-ACCESS  not-accessible
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "Primary look-up index matching the local kernel verification sequence.
         Left at Integer32 deliberately, unlike heeEpoch/contractTimeExpires:
         this counts contracts, not seconds -- ~2.1 billion signed contracts
         is not a realistic fleet-scale ceiling the way ~80 years of runway
         is for a timestamp. Open to revisiting if that reasoning is wrong."
    ::= { contractEntry 1 }

contractFileName OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      DisplayString (SIZE (1..128))
    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "Repo-relative path to the contract file, e.g.
         contracts/shift-schedule-v1.contract.yaml -- matches how contracts
         are already referenced elsewhere in this repo (see prompts/INIT.md).
         Not a hash, not an absolute path, not a URL: a path a human or
         machine can open directly from the repo root.

         'permanent state of record' here means the checked-in file on disk
         in this git repo -- disk over any remote/hosted store, per HEE's
         general preference (see docs/oper/README.md's Glossary, disk entry,
         added alongside this revision). That preference holds at every
         scale HEE runs at, hyperscaler to the pencil: the same declaration
         must stay correct whether it is read by a cloud unikernel gate or
         a human with the file printed on paper.

         128-char SIZE bound is the stored field's own limit, not a display
         limit -- for showing a long value in a UI/log, the existing
         convention in this codebase is truncate-with-both-ends
         (library/py/hee_hash/soa.py's _show(): first 8 + '..' + last 8
         chars), used today for the 64-char stool hash. Worth the same
         Glossary entry once this field's real usage proves it needs one."
    ::= { contractEntry 2 }

contractType OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      INTEGER {
                    peerToPeer(1),
                    manyToMachine(2),
                    seniorAuthority(3)
                }
    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "The hierarchical scope of authority granted to the digital execution gate.
         Open item, not resolved by this revision: whether this enum should
         instead reflect which stool-hash leg pairing (home_fs/repo_fs/user,
         see library/py/hee_hash/soa.py) authorized the contract, rather than
         a hand-picked hierarchy. Needs real iteration, flagged per PR #245
         review rather than decided unilaterally here."
    ::= { contractEntry 3 }

contractTimeExpires OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Counter64
    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "Absolute tick limit relative to the heeEpoch. If the current tick counter
         exceeds this value, authorization boundaries instantly collapse to 0.
         Widened to Counter64 to match heeEpoch above -- a narrower type here
         would just move the Y2106-class ceiling problem into the comparison
         instead of removing it."
    ::= { contractEntry 4 }

contractStatus OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      INTEGER {
                    active(1),
                    expired(2),
                    revoked(3),
                    compromised(4)
                }
    MAX-ACCESS  read-write
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "The operational state variable of the contract. Administrative scripts
         can write a value of revoked(3) to instantly lock out peripheral execution."
    ::= { contractEntry 5 }

-- Scale note (open, not resolved by this revision): the goal per PR #245
-- review is a taxonomy that stays "hee" from the most grandiose ORG down to
-- the smallest -- comparable to ORG:tcos/hee at any scale (see
-- docs/guides/EXTERNAL_SURVEY_METHODOLOGY.md's ORG term). Counter64 above
-- buys expandability past Unsigned32 for time; nothing here yet proves the
-- taxonomy itself (ownerFleetOrg / ownerHumanRightsOrg /
-- ownerMachineRightsOrg) actually scales down to something atom-sized.
-- Needs a real small-scale worked example before calling that claim proven.

END

